  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 118 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nUpper level flow becomes a bit more southwesterly tonight into \nFriday, which will allow a weak wave to drift north into the area. \nWith an elevated 1000-1500 J/kg CAPE, a freezing level around 14 kft \nand weak shear, locally heavy rain with slow moving storms will be \nthe main concern. This weak mid to upper level support lingers \ninto the afternoon and early evening, especially across parts of\nnorthwest IA, and may allow for additional showers and isolated\nthunderstorms. One note, the LLJ and 850 mb boundary looks to \nremain just south of the area so the pockets of heavier rain may\nstay just south as well. To the northwest of northwest IA weak \ncapping may keep the activity more limited. For now severe \nweather very unlikely and flash flooding threats also look low.\n\nAdditional weak mid and upper level support moves through the area \nlater Friday night into Saturday and may bring additional showers \nand isolated thunderstorms. Severe weather and flash flooding appear \nvery unlikely.\n\nOne common theme for Friday into the weekend will be persistent and \npotentially difficult to dissipate stratus and patchy fog. Weak low \nlevel flow and some residual boundary layer moisture from the latest \nrainfall may help keep this stratus potential in place until a bit \nstronger push of drier air can move into the area. Sunday does look \nlike the day with the lowest threat for any showers and storms.\n\nMonday will see a west northwest jet max sag south into the area \nwhich should allow for heating ahead with a weak cool front \ntrailing Monday night. This cool front could spark a few \nthunderstorms Monday night with isolated severe storms possible. The \nEC and Canadian are slower with this front than the GFS, so will \nneed to watch trends and for now low confidence on any storms.\n\nWest northwest flow aloft remains in place Tuesday through Thursday \nwith periodic weak waves expected to move through. This should keep \nshower and thunderstorm chances in place during this time with near \nto below normal temperatures.",
